WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.430
The first major Tai Chi movement: we are positioned here,

2
00:00:03.430 --> 00:00:05.310
performing the notochordal wave.

3
00:00:06.220 --> 00:00:09.500
We return with the entire mesodermal movement.

4
00:00:11.980 --> 00:00:16.890
The notochordal wave, and beneath it, the complete mesodermal movement.

5
00:00:16.890 --> 00:00:18.880
Next, we focus on the brain.

6
00:00:21.900 --> 00:00:23.940
1. Cerebral growth.

7
00:00:24.940 --> 00:00:27.170
2. Cephalic flexion.

8
00:00:28.062 --> 00:00:30.242
3. Cervical flexion.

9
00:00:33.922 --> 00:00:36.322
4. Pontine flexion.

10
00:00:40.062 --> 00:00:42.382
5. Telencephalization.

11
00:00:49.202 --> 00:00:53.582
Renal movement. This constitutes an external rotation movement.

12
00:00:58.825 --> 00:01:03.035
Now, we will address the bladder and uterus, and then we return.

13
00:01:08.285 --> 00:01:11.008
Peritoneum, with the right hand positioned anteriorly.

14
00:01:11.225 --> 00:01:15.177
I grasp the ansa here, drawing it towards my hepatic side.

15
00:01:15.845 --> 00:01:19.181
The hand here descends and completes the rotation in this manner.

16
00:01:20.285 --> 00:01:23.829
the ansa is positioned here before me. It expands.

17
00:01:25.528 --> 00:01:29.498
I pull this hand, locate the ansa here, and draw it towards my liver.

18
00:01:29.498 --> 00:01:33.718
Subsequently, this hand descends, ascends, and the other descends to form the

19
00:01:33.718 --> 00:01:34.560
terminal phase.

20
00:01:34.560 --> 00:01:39.149
Et puis la main ici descend, monte, et celle -là descend pour former la phase terminale.

